                <pb facs="0343" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg333"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">632.6231/174: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Brazil</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Scotten</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-06-17T13:00:00-03:00">June 17, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 17—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. My telegram No. 59, June 4, noon. The Brazilian-German compensation
                    arrangement was officially extended for a period of 3 <pb facs="0344" n="334"
                        xml:id="pg334"/> months by notes exchanged yesterday between the Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs and the German Ambassador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Scotten</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
